    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling core, anchored by **Jackson Merrill** (75.27) and **Kyle Tucker** (74.53). **Jackson Merrill** is our strongest play, benefiting from a favorable matchup against Littell (4.63 xERA) and an optimal position in the heart of the order. While the data notes a slight defensive tax for the opposition's ability to hold runners, his overall profile remains elite. Similarly, **Kyle Tucker** is in a prime spot against Painter; the combination of a generous 4.32 xERA matchup and projected wind-out conditions at the park provides an ideal environment for him to chase extra-base hits. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) also warrants mention as a high-end starter, as his platoon advantage against Canning (4.44 xERA) significantly elevates his efficiency score beyond his base projections.\n\nOur lineup construction prioritizes high-upside matchups, leaving **Josh Jung** (58.60) and **Miguel Vargas** (58.23) on the fringe of our starting rotation. **Josh Jung** was the most difficult exclusion from the top tier; his neutral platoon against Wacha keeps his floor stable, but his lack of high-end speed categories compared to others like **Sam Antonacci**\u2014whose lead-off role and 66.09 score provide better utility\u2014ultimately pushed him into the UTIL/bench consideration. We continue to monitor the status of our infirmary, as the absence of **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Jordan Westburg**, **Jorge Polanco**, and **Drake Baldwin** forces us to lean heavily on our depth. We are maintaining a cautious approach with **Brayan Rocchio** (40.91), whose position in the #9 hole against the lefty Suarez presents the lowest floor in today\u2019s active lineup. Beyond the injury list, we are tracking no significant weather-related risks, though we remain vigilant regarding the confirmed defensive alignments for those currently tagged with \"Lineup Pending.\"",
